KZ3 patch 1088 (SPU pass 67, diagnostic, opt-in): KZ3_SPU_XRSTATS=1 counts the exponent-255 recompute lanes of
patch 1071/1079 (spu__xr_fix, and the fma family's slow path) by op and operand class, by call site (the cold
function's return address, i.e. the lifted function) and by exponent-255 word; kz3_spu_xr_note in spu_drain.c prints a
summary every 2^20 lanes ([spu-xr] lines). Off by default: one load on the cold path. Results unchanged either way.

--- a/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c	2026-10-14 13:13:30.463890021 -0500
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c	2026-10-14 13:51:08.646448366 -0500
@@ -45,8 +45,100 @@
